# MI client API (CimCmdlets / Microsoft.Management.Infrastructure). Local sessions need
# the WMI provider, which is not in SysWOW64 yet, so 32-bit callers get errors, not a load failure.
SysWOW64/mi.dll
# WMI client side for 32-bit callers: the locator and its in-process provider
# (wbemprox), the scripting objects (wbemdisp, GetObject("winmgmts:") from a 32-bit
# cscript/wscript) and the path/context helpers (wmiutils). They run in the caller;
# the WMI service is not involved.
SysWOW64/wbem/wbemprox.dll
SysWOW64/wbem/wbemdisp.dll
SysWOW64/wbem/wmiutils.dll
# System.Management's native helper for 32-bit callers (the Wow6432Node .NETFramework InstallRoot).
Microsoft.NET/Framework/v4.0.30319/wminet_utils.dll
# Windows Script Host and the script engines for 32-bit scripts (GetObject("winmgmts:")
