# DLLs that Windows 10 ships in SysWOW64 and that 32-bit programs import by name (T-SYSWOW64 unbuilt-DLL follow-up):
# xinput1_4 is the first XInput library games and Chromium try; sechost, kernel.appcore and msvcp_win are forward-only
# modules; dcomp (Chrome, WinUI components of the 32-bit Firefox) and bcp47langs fail every call, so that
# the importers take their fallback.
SysWOW64/xinput1_4.dll
SysWOW64/sechost.dll
SysWOW64/kernel.appcore.dll
@0x600 SysWOW64/msvcp_win.dll
@0x601 SysWOW64/dcomp.dll
@0x601 SysWOW64/bcp47langs.dll

# The Windows 10 system ICU (icu.dll and the icuuc/icuin forwarders); the 32-bit set shares the data file
# %SystemRoot%\Globalization\ICU\icudtl.dat with the 64-bit one. The 32-bit Windows Terminal / .NET import icu.dll.
@0x600 SysWOW64/icu.dll
@0x600 SysWOW64/icuuc.dll
@0x600 SysWOW64/icuin.dll

# Microsoft 365 Apps: Repoman of the Click-to-Run client delay-loads the Restart Manager before it stages files.
SysWOW64/rstrtmgr.dll

# Microsoft 365 Apps: the Click-to-Run InspectorOfficeGadget.exe (a 32-bit AnyCPU run on WoW64) lists and removes provisioned AppX packages through the DISM API.
SysWOW64/dismapi.dll

# The .NET Framework resolves Windows Runtime types (32-bit InspectorOfficeGadget.exe of Microsoft 365 Apps) through RoResolveNamespace and the WinMetadata files; Windows has the files in both directories.
SysWOW64/wintypes.dll
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.Foundation.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.ApplicationModel.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.ApplicationModel.Activation.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.ApplicationModel.Background.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.ApplicationModel.Core.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.Devices.Geolocation.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.Devices.Input.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.Management.Deployment.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.Storage.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.Storage.FileProperties.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.Storage.Search.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.Storage.Streams.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.System.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.UI.winmd
SysWOW64/WinMetadata/Windows.UI.Input.winmd
